685
00:27:03.230 --> 00:27:04.290
The meat of the episode.

686
00:27:04.290 --> 00:27:09.930
I have a call sheet tidbit and a quote of the day from my digital clutter.

687
00:27:10.230 --> 00:27:10.730
Whoa.

688
00:27:10.990 --> 00:27:11.290
Okay.

689
00:27:11.630 --> 00:27:12.010
Uh-huh.

690
00:27:12.430 --> 00:27:13.570
I've been real excited.

691
00:27:13.570 --> 00:27:14.510
You are real excited.

692
00:27:14.510 --> 00:27:15.530
I am real excited.

693
00:27:15.850 --> 00:27:21.050
First of all, per the call sheet, we filmed this episode the week of December 10th, 2012.

694
00:27:21.610 --> 00:27:23.030
And here's your weather report.

695
00:27:23.270 --> 00:27:26.490
The week started with partly cloudy skies and a high of 72.

696
00:27:26.490 --> 00:27:31.770
And halfway through production, we were dealing with rain and highs in the 50s.

697
00:27:31.910 --> 00:27:33.770
That sounds like December in L.A.

698
00:27:33.870 --> 00:27:34.410
It does.

699
00:27:34.650 --> 00:27:37.850
But, you know, I always love that Steve Burgess sends us the call sheets, Jenna.

700
00:27:37.970 --> 00:27:38.230
Mm-hmm.

701
00:27:38.230 --> 00:27:43.890
And I immediately look at the date that we started filming, and I go to my digital clutter every week.

702
00:27:43.930 --> 00:27:47.010
And sometimes there's something there, sometimes there's not.

